{"role":"assistant","content":"Done. The full write-up is in `ANSWER.md`; here's the essence.\n\n**Why you never heard anything — two independent failures stacking:**\n\n1. **The script died before its own failure handler.** `nightly-review.zsh:19` did `status=$?`, but `status` is a read-only special variable in zsh (its name for `$?`). The assignment aborts the script on the spot — I reproduced it. So in all 6 runs, `notify.sh` was never reached. The err log shows the exact fingerprint six times: `Not logged in · Please run /login` followed by `read-only variable: status`, and launchd's `last exit code = 1` is the killed script, not claude.\n2. **Why it failed every night in the first place:** claude keeps its OAuth token in the macOS Keychain, and a process tree rooted at launchd can't use it — it reports \"Not logged in\" even with valid keychain credentials ([anthropics/claude-code#77213](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/77213)). Interactive `/login` won't fix this; the durable fix is `claude setup-token` feeding `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` to the job.\n3. **Latent:** `notify.sh` would have muted the failure note anyway — `set -e` made a failed keychain read exit wordlessly, and `curl` without `--fail` exits 0 on Telegram HTTP errors.\n\n**What I changed** (scripts only; the plist was fine):\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh` — renamed `status` → `rc`; if `notify.sh` fails, the unsent message is echoed to stderr (lands in `nightly-review.err`); sources `~/.config/nightly-review.env` when present and exports it to `claude`.\n- `bin/notify.sh` — loud, explicit keychain-read failure; `curl --fail`.\n\n**Verified offline** with stubbed `claude`/`security`/`curl`: the old script reproduces the silent death; the fixed script delivers `nightly review FAILED (exit 1), see …` on claude failure, delivers summaries on success, and leaves a clear stderr trace when the keychain or Telegram is unreachable. Harness cleaned up afterwards.\n\n**One step only you can do** (needs your claude.ai account, so out of bounds here): run `claude setup-token`, put the token in `~/.config/nightly-review.env` (`chmod 600`), then `launchctl kickstart -p gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review` to test without waiting for 02:30."}
